BT 1 0 0 1 0 109 Tm /F2 11 Tf 15 TL (The catalogue exercise applied ES6 arrow functions, callback functions, arrays and browser events to real) Tj T* (spice-export data. Array methods separated data selection from card rendering: filter\(\) narrowed the) Tj T* (catalogue, map\(\) produced the visible product entries, and reduce\(\) supported a simple summary. Input and) Tj T* (button events connected those transformations to the buyer\222s actions, while popup examples demonstrated) Tj T* (ways to request confirmation or a short value. The visible catalogue and filtered state provide practical output) Tj T* (for the report. Product data still comes from a local array, so the interactions do not depend on a backend or) Tj T* (save an enquiry. This experiment prepared the data-rendering and event-handling ideas used by later React) Tj T* (components.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 56.16 101.8982 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 64 Tm /F2 11 Tf 15 TL (The examples keep calculations close to their purpose and use clear event handlers so the catalogue can be) Tj T* (extended without mixing every action into one callback. Search terms should be normalized before) Tj T* (comparison, category filters should combine with rather than overwrite search, and the empty state should) Tj T* (explain how to broaden the query. These decisions make the JavaScript demonstrations relevant to an actual) Tj T* (buyer-facing product list.) Tj T* ET
