q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 94 Tm /F2 11 Tf 15 TL (The API design treats products and sample requests as resources and assigns HTTP methods to their) Tj T* (operations. Express routes expose public health and product-reading paths, sample creation, and protected) Tj T* (management actions. Controllers validate input and use Mongoose models; middleware handles JSON) Tj T* (parsing, CORS, authorization and consistent errors. The project Postman collection records requests for) Tj T* (repeatable checks. The local backend\222s health and unknown-route responses were tested in a browser,) Tj T* (showing a real 200 response and a real 404 response. Product and sample database operations require the) Tj T* (MongoDB service, and admin requests additionally require a private key.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 56.16 459.4898 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 4 Tm /F3 12 Tf 16 TL (Theory:) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 56.16 425.4898 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 19 Tm /F2 11 Tf 15 TL (REST represents resources at URLs and uses GET, POST, PUT and DELETE to read, create, update and) Tj T* (remove data.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 56.16 389.4898 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 19 Tm /F2 11 Tf 15 TL (HTTP status codes report outcomes: 200 for successful reads, 201 for creation, 400 for invalid input, 404 for) Tj T* (missing routes or records, and 500 for unexpected errors.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 56.16 353.4898 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 19 Tm /F2 11 Tf 15 TL (Postman sends requests and displays status and JSON responses. Admin keys belong in private local) Tj T* (variables and must not appear in screenshots.) Tj T* ET
Q
